HST Office: closing a Slides document with media from another thread no longer crashes (Windows).

DrawViewShell's destructor resets mpDrawView (null while the DrawView is destroyed) and then destroys the
windows. Destroying the media objects' system child windows from a thread other than the main one goes through
WinSalInstance::SendComWndMessage, which releases the SolarMutex while the main thread handles the message; the
main thread's idle then painted the shell's window and DrawViewShell::PrePaint called the null view: access
violation in SdrPaintView::PrePaint from vcl::Window::ImplCallPaint. Seen on Windows with 1.0.2 when a document with
linked video and audio, played for about 100 seconds, is closed through UNO (XCloseable::close from a script or
add-in), 3 times out of 3; closing it with the window's close button (main thread) did not crash. Paint and PrePaint
of a shell without its view now do nothing.

